checklist.md:99 — "`lib/pageCache.ts`'s render failures are silently swallowed — a failed thumbnail render is tracked internally (`isFailed()`) but never surfaced anywhere in the UI, so a systemic failure (e.g. `pdftoppm` missing) looks like thumbnails just never load, with no explanation. Needs a real UX design (e.g. a per-thumbnail broken-image indicator) rather than routing it through the generic unexpected-error notification, since a batch of concurrent failures across visible thumbnails would otherwise pop many persistent notifications at once."

## Current state (already investigated, don't re-explore from scratch)

`frontend/src/lib/pageCache.ts` (86 lines) is a module-level singleton cache with `entries`/`loading`/`failed` Maps keyed by `path\0page`, plus a `listeners` Set and `subscribe`/`usePageCacheRender` for React re-render notification. Full current content:

```ts
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'
import { RenderPage } from '../../wailsjs/go/main/App'

interface Entry { src: string; width: number }

const entries = new Map<string, Entry>()
const loading = new Map<string, number>()
const failed = new Map<string, number>()
const listeners = new Set<() => void>()

const pageKey = (path: string, page: number) => `${path}\0${page}`

function notify() {
  for (const fn of listeners) fn()
}

export function subscribe(fn: () => void): () => void {
  listeners.add(fn)
  return () => listeners.delete(fn)
}

export function usePageCacheRender() {
  const [, setTick] = useState(0)
  useEffect(() => subscribe(() => setTick(t => t + 1)), [])
}

export function getSrc(path: string, page: number): string | undefined {
  return entries.get(pageKey(path, page))?.src
}

export function getCachedWidth(path: string, page: number): number | undefined {
  return entries.get(pageKey(path, page))?.width
}

export function isLoading(path: string, page: number): boolean {
  return loading.has(pageKey(path, page))
}

export function isFailed(path: string, page: number): boolean {
  return failed.has(pageKey(path, page))
}

export function load(path: string, page: number, width: number): void {
  if (!path) return
  const k = pageKey(path, page)
  const existing = entries.get(k)
  if (existing && existing.width >= width) return
  const currentlyLoading = loading.get(k)
  if (currentlyLoading !== undefined && currentlyLoading >= width) return
  const failedAt = failed.get(k)
  if (failedAt !== undefined && failedAt >= width) return
  loading.set(k, width)
  RenderPage(path, page, Math.round(width * window.devicePixelRatio))
    .then((b64) => {
      const current = entries.get(k)
      if (!current || current.width <= width) {
        entries.set(k, { src: `data:image/png;base64,${b64}`, width })
      }
      if (loading.get(k) === width) loading.delete(k)
      notify()
    })
    .catch(() => {
      if (loading.get(k) === width) {
        loading.delete(k)
        failed.set(k, width)
      }
      notify()
    })
}

export function evict(path: string): void {
  const prefix = path + '\0'
  for (const k of entries.keys()) if (k.startsWith(prefix)) entries.delete(k)
  for (const k of loading.keys()) if (k.startsWith(prefix)) loading.delete(k)
  for (const k of failed.keys()) if (k.startsWith(prefix)) failed.delete(k)
  notify()
}
```

Key gaps confirmed by prior exploration:
- `failed` map stores only the failed `width`, not the error message/`Error` object — the `.catch` discards it.
- `isFailed()` is exported but **zero** current call sites read it.
- `load()` permanently no-ops once `failed.get(k) >= width` — there's no way to retry at the *same* width; only a request at a strictly higher width bypasses the failed guard. No `retry`-style function exists.
- 8 render-path consumers all follow the same shape: call `usePageCacheRender()` once, `pageCache.load(path, page, width)` in a `useEffect`, then read `getSrc`/`isLoading` — none read `isFailed`.

`frontend/src/components/PageThumbnail.tsx` (133 lines) — the small square thumbnail used by `SplitMode/ThumbnailPanel.tsx`, `MergeMode/ThumbnailPanel.tsx`, and `DriveUploadMode/components/ThumbnailPanel.tsx`. The relevant slot (lines 39-53):

```tsx
<div className={styles.imageContainer}>
  {src ? (
    <img src={src} alt={`page ${page}`} className={styles.image}
      style={{ opacity: isSkipped ? 0.3 : 1, transform: imgTransform }} draggable={false} />
  ) : (
    <div className={styles.placeholder} style={{ height: thumbHeight }}>
      {pageCache.isLoading(pdfPath, page) && <Loader size="xs" />}
    </div>
  )}
</div>
```
`pdfPath` and `page` are already props on `PageThumbnail`, so it can call `pageCache.isFailed(pdfPath, page)` itself — no new prop threading needed for the failed flag itself. It already imports `IconRotateClockwise, IconX, IconArrowUp, IconArrowDown` from `@tabler/icons-react` and uses Mantine `Loader`.

`frontend/src/components/DetailPanel.tsx` (71 lines) — the large single-page preview. Currently, if `isLoading` is false and `src` is undefined (i.e. failed, or not yet requested), the panel renders **completely blank** — no loader, no error, nothing:
```tsx
<div className={styles.panel}>
  {pageCache.isLoading(pdfPath, pageNum) && (
    <Center className={styles.loaderCenter}><Loader /></Center>
  )}
  {src && (
    <TransformWrapper ...><TransformComponent ...><img src={src} .../></TransformComponent></TransformWrapper>
  )}
</div>
```

App-wide precedent for hover-explained warning icons:
- `MergeMode/index.tsx` (~line 108-114): `<Tooltip label="..." multiline w={280}><IconAlertTriangle size={18} color="var(--mantine-color-yellow-6)" /></Tooltip>` for a page-count-mismatch warning.
- `DriveUploadMode/components/FileList.tsx` (~line 67-70): `<Tooltip label="Could not read this file — it may be corrupt or not a valid PDF"><span>⚠️</span></Tooltip>` for a corrupt-file badge (uses a bare emoji, not a tabler icon — checklist.md already flags this as inconsistent and wants it migrated to tabler icons, so a *new* failed-thumbnail indicator should use a tabler icon, not emoji).
- `frontend/src/components/TruncatedText.tsx` and `ClippedPath.tsx` establish the app's standard tooltip idiom: `<Tooltip label={...} openDelay={500}>`.
- `DriveUploadMode/components/UploadModal.tsx` (~line 105-114) has the app's only existing "failed + Retry" precedent, but it's a full list-row layout (icon/text/Retry button in a `Group`), driven by `uploadQueue`'s per-entry `error: string` field and a `retry(entry)` function — relevant as a *conceptual* precedent (store the message, expose a retry action) but not directly reusable JSX since thumbnails are tiny fixed-height squares, not rows.

checklist.md explicitly says a batch of concurrent failures across visible thumbnails should NOT pop many persistent global notifications (ruling out routing through `handleUnexpectedError`/`frontend/src/lib/globalErrorHandler.tsx`'s Mantine `notifications.show` for this case) — the fix must be localized per-thumbnail/per-panel UI, not global toasts.

